# K0: Codex findings whose quoted ranges are not co-located with any primary/replica record (never in a multi-run region).
# Each is normalized to the claim it attributes to the quoted text; all remain singletons (NO_CO_LOCATED_RECORD_FROM_OTHER_RUN).
CX X:BF-K0-0041 | The Serilog bootstrap example logs a fatal startup failure without rethrowing or setting a failure exit code (reported failure-visibility uncertainty).
CX X:BF-K0-0044 | The C# property example trims and rejects blank names silently (reported copy risk for unapproved string semantics).
CX X:BF-K0-0055 | The error-handling example maps request cancellation to status 499 (reported as a status choice beyond the cancellation rule).
CX X:BF-K0-0063 | The output-cache example embeds a five-minute TTL without a local illustrative-value caveat (reported copy risk).
CX X:BF-K0-0093 | The hosting rule file's path globs do not match repository-root Dockerfiles (reported trigger gap).
CX X:BF-K0-0098 | The backend testing rule file loads only for Tests-named directories and projects (reported trigger gap).
CX X:BF-K0-0103 | The common security rule file's path globs omit root scripts and many documentation files (reported trigger gap).
CX X:BF-K0-0106 | Literal shell comment markers ('# add-dependency: reviewed', '# project-references: approved') certify dependency review and project-reference approval for the pre-command hook.
CX X:BF-K0-0110 | The post-change hook observes only listed manifest and instruction surfaces (no imported props, lockfiles or npm configuration) and limits non-Git observation to twenty thousand entries (reported scope gaps).
CX X:BF-K0-0111 | The post-change hook persists the observed worktree state before checking and reporting (reported: a validation failure can count as already observed on the next call).
CX X:BF-K0-0113 | Post-tool feedback emits a blocking decision for notices and reminders (reported as a workflow gate beyond relevant verification).
CX X:BF-K0-0118 | The dependency checker tracks only .csproj, Directory.Packages.props and package.json outside dot-directories and build output (reported: props/targets, lockfiles and peer dependencies are not covered).
CX X:BF-K0-0119 | The dependency checker's XML parsing does not remove comments or evaluate conditions (reported: inactive or commented references may be enforced).
CX X:BF-K0-0131 | Root resolution prefers the Git top-level over the nearest instruction-system root (reported: a surrounding monorepo may be checked instead of the nested project).
